{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349344994,"sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1776c56159ce4c8396368e02","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n2: \n3: # Task\n4: \n5: Operator: **Gelu**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `gelu` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n6: \n7: # Operator specification\n8: \n9: ## desc.md\n10: \n11: # Gelu 算子 API 描述\n12: \n13: ## 1. 算子简介\n14: \n15: Gelu（高斯误差线性单元）是一种广泛应用于 Transformer 架构的激活函数，支持精确计算和 tanh 近似两种模式。\n16: \n17: **主要应用场景**：\n18: - BERT、GPT 等 Transformer 模型的前馈网络激活层\n19: - Vision Transformer (ViT) 中的 MLP 模块\n20: - 各类预训练语言模型的中间激活\n21: \n22: **算子特征**：\n23: - 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n24: - 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n25: - 支持 0~8 维输入\n26: \n27: ## 2. 算子定义\n28: \n29: ### 数学公式\n30: \n31: **精确模式**（approximate=\"none\"）：\n32: \n33: $$\n34: y = x \\cdot \\Phi(x) = x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\left[1 + \\text{erf}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\right]\n35: $$\n36: \n37: **tanh 近似模式**（approximate=\"tanh\"）：\n38: \n39: $$\n40: y = 0.5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\left(1 + \\tanh\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{\\pi}} \\cdot (x + 0.044715 \\cdot x^3)\\right)\\right)\n41: $$\n42: \n43: ### 特殊情况\n44: \n45: | 输入 | 输出 |\n46: |------|------|\n47: | x = 0 | y = 0 |\n48: | x → +∞ | y → x |\n49: | x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n50: \n51: ## 3. 接口规范\n52: \n53: ### 算子原型\n54: \n55: ```python\n56: cann_bench.gelu(Tensor x, str approximate=\"none\") -> Tensor y\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ### 输入参数说明\n60: \n61: | 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n62: |------|------|--------|------|\n63: | x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 0~8 维 |\n64: | approximate | str | \"none\" | GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'（精确计算）或 'tanh'（tanh 近似） |\n65: \n66: ### 输出\n67: \n68: | 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n69: |------|-------|-------|------|\n70: | y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | GELU 激活结果 |\n71: \n72: ### 数据类型\n73: \n74: | 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n75: |-----------|-----------|\n76: | float16 | float16 |\n77: | float32 | float32 |\n78: | bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n79: \n80: ### 规则与约束\n81: \n82: - 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n83: - `approximate` 参数仅支持 \"none\" 和 \"tanh\" 两种取值\n84: - 输入支持 0~8 维\n85: \n86: ### 支持范围\n87: \n88: 输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n89: \n90: | 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n91: |---|---|---|\n92: | `x` 维度数 | 0 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1D ~ 5D；接口规范支持 0 ~ 8 维 |\n93: | `x` 各维大小 | 1 ~ 1048576 | cases.csv 各维实测 2 ~ 8192（含 1D 张量长度 1000003） |\n94: | `x` 元素总数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M |\n95: | `approximate` | {\"none\", \"tanh\"} | cases.csv 两种取值均覆盖；仅支持这两种字符串 |\n96: \n97: ## 4. 精度要求\n98: \n99: 采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n100: \n101: **误差指标**：\n102: \n103: 1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n104: \n105:    $$\n106:    \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n107:    $$\n108: \n109: 2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n110: \n111:    $$\n112:    \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n113:    $$\n114: \n115: **通过标准**：\n116: \n117: | 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n118: |----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n119: | **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n120: \n121: 当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n122: \n123: \n124: ## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n125: \n126: ```python\n127: import torch\n128: \n129: def gelu(\n130:     x: torch.Tensor,\n131:     approximate: str = \"none\"\n132: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n133:     \"\"\"\n134:     高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n135: \n136:     公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n137: \n138:     Args:\n139:         x: 输入张量\n140:         approximate: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n141: \n142:     Returns:\n143:         输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n144:     \"\"\"\n145: \n146:     y = torch.nn.functional.gelu(x, approximate=approximate)\n147:     return y\n148: ```\n149: \n150: ## 6. 额外信息\n151: \n152: ### 算子调用示例\n153: \n154: ```python\n155: import torch\n156: import cann_bench\n157: \n158: x = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\n159: y = cann_bench.gelu(x)                          # 精确模式\n160: y = cann_bench.gelu(x, approximate=\"tanh\")       # tanh 近似模式\n161: ```\n162: \n163: ## proto.yaml\n164: \n165: ```yaml\n166: operator:\n167:   name: Gelu\n168:   category: Elementwise\n169:   difficulty: L1\n170:   formula: y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n171:   description: 高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n172:   shape_support: 输入 0-8 维\n173:   attrs:\n174:   - name: approximate\n175:     type: str\n176:     default: \"none\"\n177:     description: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n178:   inputs:\n179:   - name: x\n180:     description: 输入张量\n181:     dtype:\n182:     - float32\n183:     - float16\n184:     - bfloat16\n185:   outputs:\n186:   - name: y\n187:     description: 输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n188:     dtype:\n189:     - float32\n190:     - float16\n191:     - bfloat16\n192:   schema: gelu(Tensor x, str approximate=\"none\") -> Tensor y\n193: ```\n194: \n195: ## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n196: \n197: ```python\n198: #!/usr/bin/python3\n199: # coding=utf-8\n200: \n201: \n202: import torch\n203: \n204: \"\"\"\n205: Gelu 算子 Torch Golden 参考实现\n206: \n207: 高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n208: 公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n209: \"\"\"\n210: def gelu(\n211:     x: torch.Tensor,\n212:     approximate: str = \"none\"\n213: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n214:     \"\"\"\n215:     高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n216: \n217:     公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n218: \n219:     Args:\n220:         x: 输入张量\n221:         approximate: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n222: \n223:     Returns:\n224:         输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n225:     \"\"\"\n226: \n227:     y = torch.nn.functional.gelu(x, approximate=approximate)\n228:     return y\n229: ```\n230: \n231: ## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n232: \n233: | case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n234: |---|---|---|---|---|\n235: | 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n236: | 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n237: | 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n238: | 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n239: | 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n240: | 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n241: | 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n242: | 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n243: | 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n244: | 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n245: | 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n246: | 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n247: | 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n248: | 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n249: | 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n250: | 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n251: | 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n252: | 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n253: | 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n254: | 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n255: \n256: # Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n257: \n258: ```python\n259: \"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n260: \n261: Kernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n262:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n263:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n264:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n265:     (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n266:   - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n267:     the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n268:     maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n269:   - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n270:     limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n271: \"\"\"\n272: \n273: import torch\n274: \n275: import asc\n276: import asc2\n277: \n278: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n279: \n280: _WIDE_TILE = 3072\n281: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n282: _MAX_CORES = 72\n283: \n284: \n285: @asc2.jit\n286: def _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n287:                     size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n288:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n289:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n290:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n291:                         unroll_factor=2):\n292:         off = t * tile_size\n293:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n294:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n295:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n296:         y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n297:         asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n298: \n299: \n300: def sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n301:     \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n302:     ensure_npu_platform()\n303:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n304:         x = x.contiguous()\n305:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n306:     size = x.numel()\n307:     if size == 0:\n308:         return out\n309:     if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n310:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n311:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n312:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n313:     else:\n314:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n315:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n316:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n317:     return out\n318: \n319: ```\n320: \n321: # pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n322: \n323: ## Module shape\n324: \n325: Your file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n326: \n327: - imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n328:   `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n329: - one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n330: - ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n331: - wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n332:   needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n333:   `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n334:   launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n335:   return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n336: \n337: ## Kernel authoring rules\n338: \n339: - Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n340:   `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n341:   copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n342: - Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n343:   (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n344:   value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n345: - Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n346: \n347: ```python\n348: for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n349:     off = t * tile_size\n350:     n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n351:     x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n352:     ...compute on tiles...\n353:     asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n354: ```\n355: \n356: - Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n357:   on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n358: - Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n359:   `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n360:   `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n361:   `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n362:   comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n363:   `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n364:   `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n365:   `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n366:   `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n367:   `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n368:   `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n369: - int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n370:   (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n371:   no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n372: - Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n373:   write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n374: - f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n375:   compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n376: - UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n377:   Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n378:   doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n379:   calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n380:   `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n381:   311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n382:   `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n383:   Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n384:   512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n385:   bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n386:   cases).\n387: - `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n388:   (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n389: - Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n390:   `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n391:   (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n392:   different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n393:   `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n394:   `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n395:   TypeError).\n396: - Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n397:   [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n398:   int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n399:   destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n400:   Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n401:   `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n402:   kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n403: - Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n404:   `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n405:   style (min 32 bytes).\n406: - Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n407:   `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n408:   `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n409: \n410: ## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n411: \n412: - Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n413:   nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n414:   `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n415: - Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n416:   - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n417:   - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n418:   - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n419:     `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n420:     for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n421:   - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n422:     `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n423:     the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n424: - IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n425:   through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n426:   unless the golden does.\n427: \n428: ## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n429: \n430: - ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n431: - torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n432:   `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n433:   `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n434:   `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n435: - FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n436:   `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n437:   `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n438:   `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n439:   rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n440:   is detected and scored as cheating.\n441: - Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n442:   shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n443: \n444: \n445: # Operator-specific guidance\n446: \n447: -\n448: \n449: # Deliverable\n450: \n451: Write ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `gelu` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n452: \n453: IMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.\n454: \n455: \n456: # Evaluator feedback from the previous iteration\n457: \n458: The previous three-phase workflow did not pass its mandatory skill provenance gates. Start over from the full original operator task and produce a fresh candidate.\n\n(End of file - total 458 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Gelu**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `gelu` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Gelu 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nGelu（高斯误差线性单元）是一种广泛应用于 Transformer 架构的激活函数，支持精确计算和 tanh 近似两种模式。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- BERT、GPT 等 Transformer 模型的前馈网络激活层\n- Vision Transformer (ViT) 中的 MLP 模块\n- 各类预训练语言模型的中间激活","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/task.md","text":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Gelu**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `gelu` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Gelu 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nGelu（高斯误差线性单元）是一种广泛应用于 Transformer 架构的激活函数，支持精确计算和 tanh 近似两种模式。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- BERT、GPT 等 Transformer 模型的前馈网络激活层\n- Vision Transformer (ViT) 中的 MLP 模块\n- 各类预训练语言模型的中间激活\n\n**算子特征**：\n- 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n- 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n- 支持 0~8 维输入\n\n## 2. 算子定义\n\n### 数学公式\n\n**精确模式**（approximate=\"none\"）：\n\n$$\ny = x \\cdot \\Phi(x) = x \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\left[1 + \\text{erf}\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\right]\n$$\n\n**tanh 近似模式**（approximate=\"tanh\"）：\n\n$$\ny = 0.5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\left(1 + \\tanh\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{\\pi}} \\cdot (x + 0.044715 \\cdot x^3)\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\n### 特殊情况\n\n| 输入 | 输出 |\n|------|------|\n| x = 0 | y = 0 |\n| x → +∞ | y → x |\n| x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n\n## 3. 接口规范\n\n### 算子原型\n\n```python\ncann_bench.gelu(Tensor x, str approximate=\"none\") -> Tensor y\n```\n\n### 输入参数说明\n\n| 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n|------|------|--------|------|\n| x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 0~8 维 |\n| approximate | str | \"none\" | GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'（精确计算）或 'tanh'（tanh 近似） |\n\n### 输出\n\n| 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n|------|-------|-------|------|\n| y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | GELU 激活结果 |\n\n### 数据类型\n\n| 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| float16 | float16 |\n| float32 | float32 |\n| bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n\n### 规则与约束\n\n- 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n- `approximate` 参数仅支持 \"none\" 和 \"tanh\" 两种取值\n- 输入支持 0~8 维\n\n### 支持范围\n\n输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n\n| 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `x` 维度数 | 0 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1D ~ 5D；接口规范支持 0 ~ 8 维 |\n| `x` 各维大小 | 1 ~ 1048576 | cases.csv 各维实测 2 ~ 8192（含 1D 张量长度 1000003） |\n| `x` 元素总数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M |\n| `approximate` | {\"none\", \"tanh\"} | cases.csv 两种取值均覆盖；仅支持这两种字符串 |\n\n## 4. 精度要求\n\n采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n\n**误差指标**：\n\n1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n**通过标准**：\n\n| 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n|----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n\n当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n\n\n## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef gelu(\n    x: torch.Tensor,\n    approximate: str = \"none\"\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n\n    公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n        approximate: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n\n    y = torch.nn.functional.gelu(x, approximate=approximate)\n    return y\n```\n\n## 6. 额外信息\n\n### 算子调用示例\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport cann_bench\n\nx = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\ny = cann_bench.gelu(x)                          # 精确模式\ny = cann_bench.gelu(x, approximate=\"tanh\")       # tanh 近似模式\n```\n\n## proto.yaml\n\n```yaml\noperator:\n  name: Gelu\n  category: Elementwise\n  difficulty: L1\n  formula: y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n  description: 高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n  shape_support: 输入 0-8 维\n  attrs:\n  - name: approximate\n    type: str\n    default: \"none\"\n    description: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n  inputs:\n  - name: x\n    description: 输入张量\n    dtype:\n    - float32\n    - float16\n    - bfloat16\n  outputs:\n  - name: y\n    description: 输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n    dtype:\n    - float32\n    - float16\n    - bfloat16\n  schema: gelu(Tensor x, str approximate=\"none\") -> Tensor y\n```\n\n## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n# coding=utf-8\n\n\nimport torch\n\n\"\"\"\nGelu 算子 Torch Golden 参考实现\n\n高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n\"\"\"\ndef gelu(\n    x: torch.Tensor,\n    approximate: str = \"none\"\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    高斯误差线性单元激活函数\n\n    公式：y = 0.5 * x * (1 + tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n        approximate: GELU 近似计算算法，可选值：'none'(精确计算) 或 'tanh'(tanh 近似)\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，GELU 激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n\n    y = torch.nn.functional.gelu(x, approximate=approximate)\n    return y\n```\n\n## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n\n| case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n| 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | {'approximate': 'tanh'} |\n| 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | {'approximate': 'none'} |\n\n# Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n\n```python\n\"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n    (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n  - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n    the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n    maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n  - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n    limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 3072\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n        asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n    else:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n    return out\n\n```\n\n# pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n\n## Module shape\n\nYour file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n\n- imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n  `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n- one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n- ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n- wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n  needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n  `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n  launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n  return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n\n## Kernel authoring rules\n\n- Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n  `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n  copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n- Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n  (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n  value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n- Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n\n```python\nfor t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n    off = t * tile_size\n    n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n    x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n    ...compute on tiles...\n    asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\n- Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n  on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n- Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n  `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n  `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n  `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n  comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n  `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n  `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n  `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n  `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n  `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n  `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n- int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n  (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n  no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n- Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n  write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n- f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n  compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n- UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n  Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n  doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n  calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n  `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n  311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n  `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n  Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n  512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n  bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n  cases).\n- `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n  (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n- Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n  `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n  (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n  different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n  `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n  `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n  TypeError).\n- Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n  [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n  int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n  destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n  Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n  `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n  kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n- Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n  `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n  style (min 32 bytes).\n- Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n  `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n  `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n\n## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n\n- Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n  nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n  `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n- Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n  - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n  - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n  - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n    `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n    for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n  - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n    `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n    the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n- IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n  through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n  unless the golden does.\n\n## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n\n- ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n- torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n  `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n  `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n  `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n- FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n  `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n  `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n  `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n  rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n  is detected and scored as cheating.\n- Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n  shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n\n\n# Operator-specific guidance\n\n-\n\n# Deliverable\n\nWrite ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `gelu` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n\nIMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.\n\n\n# Evaluator feedback from the previous iteration\n\nThe previous three-phase workflow did not pass its mandatory skill provenance gates. Start over from the full original operator task and produce a fresh candidate.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":458,"totalLines":458,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/task.md","time":{"start":1788349344980,"end":1788349344992}},"id":"prt_061ed6a1b001pTMJ83E1XUXkep","sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","messageID":"msg_061ed62c2001nXJqo8f5ijtwTT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349345681,"sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_87572fcf9ce04bd19af64eb3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/design.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/design.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n2: \n3: Provenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n4: = `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\n5: run artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n6: \n7: ## 1. Algorithm\n8: \n9: Public callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n10: `approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\n11: Dispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\n12: Both kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n13: \n14: - **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n15:   `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n16: - **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n17:   `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n18:   `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n19:   Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n20: \n21: All constants are module-level floats (no `math.*` inside jit). Scalars always on the\n22: RIGHT of tile arithmetic (`x*C1`, `t+1.0`, `x*0.5`) — `Tile.__rmul__` is absent.\n23: \n24: ## 2. Pinned v2 APIs (CANNBench contract)\n25: \n26: - `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform`\n27: - `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D GM view (rank-1 throughout; no 2-D mix).\n28: - `asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])` — tile load with tail.\n29: - `asc2.copy_out(y_cast, out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` — tile store with tail.\n30: - `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` — grid-stride.\n31: - `asc.GlobalAddress` for ptrs; `int` for size/num_tiles; `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile size.\n32: - Casts: `x.to(asc.float32)`, `y.to(x.dtype)`. Math: `asc2.erf`, `asc2.tanh`, `+ *`.\n33: - Launch: `kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, TILE)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`.\n34: - Target: `Ascend950PR_9599`, 72 AIV cores, UB 253952 B.\n35: \n36: ## 3. All 20 cases (coverage)\n37: \n38: 1-D flatten + grid-stride + `real_shape` tails covers every rank (1D–5D present;\n39: spec 0–8D) and every odd/non-multiple shape. No host shape branch needed.\n40: \n41: | # | shape | dtype | range | mode | elems | path |\n42: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n43: |1|[1024,1024]|f16|[-1,1]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n44: |2|[2048,2048]|f32|[-2,2]|erf|4.19M|erf|\n45: |3|[4096,4096]|bf16|[-3,3]|erf|16.78M|erf|\n46: |4|[8192,8192]|f16|[-10,10]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n47: |5|[8192,8192]|f32|[-100,100]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n48: |6|[1023,1023]|bf16|[-0.1,0.1]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n49: |7|[1009,1021]|f16|[-1,2]|erf|1.03M|erf|\n50: |8|[1537,769]|f32|[-5,10]|tanh|1.18M|tanh|\n51: |9|[363,367,373]|bf16|[-50,100]|erf|49.9M|erf|\n52: |10|[2049,513]|f16|[-65504,65504]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n53: |11|[3,7,13,4001]|f32|[-88,88]|erf|1.09M|erf|\n54: |12|[1000003]|bf16|[-inf,inf]|tanh|1.00M|tanh|\n55: |13|[11,13,17,67,67]|f32|[nan,nan]|erf|10.9M|erf|\n56: |14|[3,7,11,13,1009]|f16|[0,0]|tanh|3.03M|tanh|\n57: |15|[512,2049]|f32|[-0.5,0.5]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n58: |16|[255,8193]|bf16|[-1,3]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n59: |17|[4097,511]|f16|[-1000,1000]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n60: |18|[2,511,2049]|f32|[-0.2,0.2]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n61: |19|[4,255,2049]|bf16|[-3,6]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n62: |20|[2,3,17,1024,101]|f32|[-20,40]|erf|10.5M|erf|\n63: \n64: All cases ≥ ~1.0M elems ⇒ all take the wide tile path; narrow path retained only for\n65: spec-completeness on tiny/empty tensors (`size == 0` → return `empty_like`).\n66: \n67: ## 4. Tiling & tails\n68: \n69: Two kernels (separate JIT cache entries, minimal UB per path):\n70: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, each grid-stride:\n71: \n72: ```\n73: for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n74:     off = t * tile\n75:     n = tile if off + tile <= size else size - off     # tail\n76:     x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])\n77:     xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n78:     ...compute yf in f32...\n79:     asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n80: ```\n81: \n82: Tiles (pinned, see §5):\n83: - `_ERF_TILE  = 2048` (wide), `_NARROW = 1024`.\n84: - `_TANH_TILE = 1024` (wide == narrow; tanh chain is longer).\n85: - `_MAX_CORES = 72`; threshold `_MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE = 147456`.\n86: \n87: Dispatch:\n88: - `size == 0` → `return torch.empty_like(x)`.\n89: - erf: `size >= threshold` → TILE=2048 else 1024; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,TILE))`.\n90: - tanh: TILE=1024 always; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,1024))`.\n91: \n92: ## 5. UB budget (253952 B, static alloc)\n93: \n94: Formula (measured calibration from the sigmoid reference on this build): \n95: `real ≈ 1.6 * V * 4 * TILE * unroll(=2)`, where `V` = #live f32 tile values.\n96: \n97: - **erf chain** `V ≈ 6` (`xf, s, e, one, hx, y`) + input-dtype load/store.\n98:   erf@2048 u2: `1.6*6*4*2048*2 = 157286 B` ✓ (96 KB headroom; matches the proven\n99:   sigmoid chain length, and gives margin for any hidden erf temporaries).\n100: - **tanh chain** `V ≈ 10` (`xf, x2, x3, a, b, c, t, one, hx, y`).\n101:   tanh@2048 u2: `1.6*10*4*2048*2 = 262144 B` ✗ (8 KB over ⇒ launch-time `UB overflow`).\n102:   tanh@1536 u2: `1.6*10*4*1536*2 = 196608 B` ✓ (57 KB / 23% headroom).\n103:   tanh@1024 u2: `1.6*10*4*1024*2 = 131072 B` ✓ (122 KB headroom).\n104:   **Pinned: tanh TILE = 1024** — chosen for one-shot safety (no local NPU to probe\n105:   hidden temporaries of the `tanh`/`mul` chain); 1536 is a perf fallback if a local\n106:   compile gate were available. UB overflow is a **runtime** launch failure (not caught\n107:   by the exact-v2 compile gate), so conservative is correct here.\n108: \n109: 256-byte alignment rule: `TILE*4 % 256 == 0` ⇒ `TILE % 64 == 0`; 2048 and 1024 both OK.\n110: \n111: ## 6. Numerical risks\n112: \n113: - **x³ overflow**: max |x| in tanh cases is 65504 (case 10, f16→f32). `65504³ ≈ 2.8e14`,\n114:   well within f32 (max ~3.4e38). case 17 (±1000) → 1e9. No overflow.\n115: - **tanh saturation**: `tanh(large)=±1`; for large |x|, `K*x³` dominates, `x` is lost in\n116:   `x + K*x³` (catastrophic cancellation) **but** tanh has already saturated to ±1, so\n117:   `y = 0.5*x*(±1+1) = x or 0` — the cancellation is benign and matches golden, which\n118:   uses the identical formula. No special-case branch.\n119: - **erf saturation**: `erf(|x|/√2)`→±1 for |x|≳6 (cases 9,11,20). `asc2.erf` is a vector\n120:   op on this build; saturation gives correct limits `y→x` (+∞), `y→0` (−∞).\n121: - **Inf (case 12 bf16 [−inf,inf])**: IEEE propagation — `x=+inf ⇒ x³=inf ⇒ c=inf ⇒\n122:   tanh=1 ⇒ y=+inf`; `x=−inf ⇒ c=−inf ⇒ tanh=−1 ⇒ 0.5*(−inf)*0 = NaN`. Golden\n123:   (`torch.nn.functional.gelu`) computes the same expression and yields the same IEEE\n124:   result ⇒ relative-error match (golden-equal). Documented as a residual `suspected`\n125:   risk if the harness treats `NaN≠NaN`; cannot be special-cased without diverging from\n126:   golden.\n127: - **NaN (case 13 f32 [nan,nan])**: `erf(NaN)=NaN`, `0.5*NaN*(1+NaN)=NaN`. IEEE\n128:   propagation through `asc2.erf`/mul ⇒ matches golden. Same residual NaN-comparison\n129:   caveat as above.\n130: - **Zero (case 14 [0,0] tanh)**: `erf/tanh(0)=0`, `y=0`. Exact.\n131: - **Precision**: f16 thresh `2^-10≈9.7e-4`, bf16 `2^-7≈7.8e-3`, f32 `2^-13≈1.2e-4`.\n132:   All f16/bf16 cases compute in f32 then cast back ⇒ strictly more accurate than the\n133:   golden's f16/bf16 path; f32 cases use the cancellation-free erf/tanh forms with no\n134:   `exp(+arg)` (no overflow) and no `log(1+tiny)` (no flush). `erf`/`tanh` are bounded,\n135:   so no guard-band logic is needed.\n136: \n137: ## 7. Anti-cheat constraints\n138: \n139: - ALL math (`erf`, `tanh`, `*`, `+`, casts) lives inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on\n140:   the NPU. Host does only: `ensure_npu_platform()`, `.contiguous()`, `torch.empty_like`,\n141:   `.numel()`, `.dtype`, string dispatch, launch, return.\n142: - No torch compute/math ops anywhere (`torch.mul`, `F.gelu`, `a+b`, `.to(dtype)` on\n143:   device data, `torch.cat/clone/sum`, `x.sigmoid()`…). No `data_ptr` caching.\n144: - `approximate` string is consumed on the host only (never passed into a kernel — str\n145:   is not a supported param type anyway).\n146: - Output is a fresh contiguous NPU tensor (`torch.empty_like(x)`) with golden's exact\n147:   shape/dtype; no views of the input.\n148: - Constants precomputed module-level; no `import`/`math.*` inside jit.\n149: \n150: ## 8. Local validation ladder\n151: \n152: No NPU and no pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu installed locally (per task.md). Ladder:\n153: \n154: 1. **Syntax only** — `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (allowed; checks AST, no\n155:    imports execute). Run after writing candidate.\n156: 2. **Worker static contract check** — requires the CANNBench worker runtime; not\n157:    runnable here ⇒ treated as `suspected`, deferred to remote.\n158: 3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** (skill `references/local-validation.md`) — requires\n159:    the pinned `pyasc-v2-source`; not installed here ⇒ `suspected`, deferred. UB\n160:    overflow (§5) is a runtime launch failure that this gate would NOT catch anyway;\n161:    the conservative tiles in §4 are chosen to avoid it a priori.\n162: 4. **camodel numerical compare vs golden.py** — no local camodel ⇒ `suspected`.\n163: 5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — the only acceptance/performance oracle; remote, invoked\n164:    by the official harness.\n165: \n166: Evidence label for the design phase: `suspected` (no local compile/numerical evidence\n167: possible). Promotion to `verified-local-compile` / `verified-camodel` requires steps\n168: 2–4, which are unavailable in this environment.\n169: \n170: ## 9. Open implementation notes (for candidate.py, next phase)\n171: \n172: - Two kernels: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, identical signature\n173:   `(x: asc.GlobalAddress, out: asc.GlobalAddress, size: int, num_tiles: int,\n174:    tile: asc.ConstExpr[int])`.\n175: - Host `gelu(x, approximate=\"none\")`: `ensure_npu_platform()`; `if not x.is_contiguous():\n176:   x = x.contiguous()`; `out = torch.empty_like(x)`; `size = x.numel()`; empty→return;\n177:   branch on `approximate` (`\"none\"`→erf, `\"tanh\"`→tanh; any other value ⇒ assert, since\n178:   spec allows only these two); pick tile per §4; `ceildiv` via `asc.ceildiv`;\n179:   `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`; launch; return `out`.\n180: - `x.is_contiguous()` / `.contiguous()` / `.numel()` / `.dtype` are metadata/views —\n181:   allowed by the anti-cheat whitelist.\n182: \n183: DESIGN_DONE\n\n(End of file - total 183 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n\nProvenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n= `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\nrun artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n\n## 1. Algorithm\n\nPublic callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n`approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\nDispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\nBoth kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n\n- **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n  `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n- **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n  `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n  `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n  Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/design.md","text":"# design.md — Gelu (CANNBench, pyasc asc2)\n\nProvenance: skills `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` + `pyasc-syntax-constraints` loaded; context\n= `task.md` (desc/proto/golden/20 cases + kernel contract) only. No submission modules,\nrun artifacts, or pyasc source inspected. `candidate.py` not yet written.\n\n## 1. Algorithm\n\nPublic callable `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n`approximate` is a **str** → unsupported as a kernel param (type constraints).\nDispatch on the host string and launch one of two specialized `@asc2.jit` kernels.\nBoth kernels flatten to 1-D (`numel`), promote f16/bf16→f32, compute, cast back.\n\n- **erf mode** (`approximate == \"none\"`): `y = (x*0.5) * (erf(x*C1) + 1.0)`,\n  `C1 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476`.\n- **tanh mode** (`approximate == \"tanh\"`):\n  `y = (x*0.5) * (tanh(C0 * (x + K*x*x*x)) + 1.0)`,\n  `C0 = sqrt(2/pi) = 0.7978845608028654`, `K = 0.044715`.\n  Compute order: `x2=x*x; x3=x2*x; a=x3*K; b=x+a; c=b*C0; t=tanh(c); one=t+1.0; hx=x*0.5; y=hx*one`.\n\nAll constants are module-level floats (no `math.*` inside jit). Scalars always on the\nRIGHT of tile arithmetic (`x*C1`, `t+1.0`, `x*0.5`) — `Tile.__rmul__` is absent.\n\n## 2. Pinned v2 APIs (CANNBench contract)\n\n- `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform`\n- `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D GM view (rank-1 throughout; no 2-D mix).\n- `asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])` — tile load with tail.\n- `asc2.copy_out(y_cast, out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` — tile store with tail.\n- `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` — grid-stride.\n- `asc.GlobalAddress` for ptrs; `int` for size/num_tiles; `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile size.\n- Casts: `x.to(asc.float32)`, `y.to(x.dtype)`. Math: `asc2.erf`, `asc2.tanh`, `+ *`.\n- Launch: `kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, TILE)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`.\n- Target: `Ascend950PR_9599`, 72 AIV cores, UB 253952 B.\n\n## 3. All 20 cases (coverage)\n\n1-D flatten + grid-stride + `real_shape` tails covers every rank (1D–5D present;\nspec 0–8D) and every odd/non-multiple shape. No host shape branch needed.\n\n| # | shape | dtype | range | mode | elems | path |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|[1024,1024]|f16|[-1,1]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n|2|[2048,2048]|f32|[-2,2]|erf|4.19M|erf|\n|3|[4096,4096]|bf16|[-3,3]|erf|16.78M|erf|\n|4|[8192,8192]|f16|[-10,10]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n|5|[8192,8192]|f32|[-100,100]|tanh|67.1M|tanh|\n|6|[1023,1023]|bf16|[-0.1,0.1]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n|7|[1009,1021]|f16|[-1,2]|erf|1.03M|erf|\n|8|[1537,769]|f32|[-5,10]|tanh|1.18M|tanh|\n|9|[363,367,373]|bf16|[-50,100]|erf|49.9M|erf|\n|10|[2049,513]|f16|[-65504,65504]|tanh|1.05M|tanh|\n|11|[3,7,13,4001]|f32|[-88,88]|erf|1.09M|erf|\n|12|[1000003]|bf16|[-inf,inf]|tanh|1.00M|tanh|\n|13|[11,13,17,67,67]|f32|[nan,nan]|erf|10.9M|erf|\n|14|[3,7,11,13,1009]|f16|[0,0]|tanh|3.03M|tanh|\n|15|[512,2049]|f32|[-0.5,0.5]|erf|1.05M|erf|\n|16|[255,8193]|bf16|[-1,3]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n|17|[4097,511]|f16|[-1000,1000]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n|18|[2,511,2049]|f32|[-0.2,0.2]|erf|2.09M|erf|\n|19|[4,255,2049]|bf16|[-3,6]|tanh|2.09M|tanh|\n|20|[2,3,17,1024,101]|f32|[-20,40]|erf|10.5M|erf|\n\nAll cases ≥ ~1.0M elems ⇒ all take the wide tile path; narrow path retained only for\nspec-completeness on tiny/empty tensors (`size == 0` → return `empty_like`).\n\n## 4. Tiling & tails\n\nTwo kernels (separate JIT cache entries, minimal UB per path):\n`_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, each grid-stride:\n\n```\nfor t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n    off = t * tile\n    n = tile if off + tile <= size else size - off     # tail\n    x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile], real_shape=[n])\n    xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n    ...compute yf in f32...\n    asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\nTiles (pinned, see §5):\n- `_ERF_TILE  = 2048` (wide), `_NARROW = 1024`.\n- `_TANH_TILE = 1024` (wide == narrow; tanh chain is longer).\n- `_MAX_CORES = 72`; threshold `_MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE = 147456`.\n\nDispatch:\n- `size == 0` → `return torch.empty_like(x)`.\n- erf: `size >= threshold` → TILE=2048 else 1024; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,TILE))`.\n- tanh: TILE=1024 always; `cores=min(72, ceildiv(size,1024))`.\n\n## 5. UB budget (253952 B, static alloc)\n\nFormula (measured calibration from the sigmoid reference on this build): \n`real ≈ 1.6 * V * 4 * TILE * unroll(=2)`, where `V` = #live f32 tile values.\n\n- **erf chain** `V ≈ 6` (`xf, s, e, one, hx, y`) + input-dtype load/store.\n  erf@2048 u2: `1.6*6*4*2048*2 = 157286 B` ✓ (96 KB headroom; matches the proven\n  sigmoid chain length, and gives margin for any hidden erf temporaries).\n- **tanh chain** `V ≈ 10` (`xf, x2, x3, a, b, c, t, one, hx, y`).\n  tanh@2048 u2: `1.6*10*4*2048*2 = 262144 B` ✗ (8 KB over ⇒ launch-time `UB overflow`).\n  tanh@1536 u2: `1.6*10*4*1536*2 = 196608 B` ✓ (57 KB / 23% headroom).\n  tanh@1024 u2: `1.6*10*4*1024*2 = 131072 B` ✓ (122 KB headroom).\n  **Pinned: tanh TILE = 1024** — chosen for one-shot safety (no local NPU to probe\n  hidden temporaries of the `tanh`/`mul` chain); 1536 is a perf fallback if a local\n  compile gate were available. UB overflow is a **runtime** launch failure (not caught\n  by the exact-v2 compile gate), so conservative is correct here.\n\n256-byte alignment rule: `TILE*4 % 256 == 0` ⇒ `TILE % 64 == 0`; 2048 and 1024 both OK.\n\n## 6. Numerical risks\n\n- **x³ overflow**: max |x| in tanh cases is 65504 (case 10, f16→f32). `65504³ ≈ 2.8e14`,\n  well within f32 (max ~3.4e38). case 17 (±1000) → 1e9. No overflow.\n- **tanh saturation**: `tanh(large)=±1`; for large |x|, `K*x³` dominates, `x` is lost in\n  `x + K*x³` (catastrophic cancellation) **but** tanh has already saturated to ±1, so\n  `y = 0.5*x*(±1+1) = x or 0` — the cancellation is benign and matches golden, which\n  uses the identical formula. No special-case branch.\n- **erf saturation**: `erf(|x|/√2)`→±1 for |x|≳6 (cases 9,11,20). `asc2.erf` is a vector\n  op on this build; saturation gives correct limits `y→x` (+∞), `y→0` (−∞).\n- **Inf (case 12 bf16 [−inf,inf])**: IEEE propagation — `x=+inf ⇒ x³=inf ⇒ c=inf ⇒\n  tanh=1 ⇒ y=+inf`; `x=−inf ⇒ c=−inf ⇒ tanh=−1 ⇒ 0.5*(−inf)*0 = NaN`. Golden\n  (`torch.nn.functional.gelu`) computes the same expression and yields the same IEEE\n  result ⇒ relative-error match (golden-equal). Documented as a residual `suspected`\n  risk if the harness treats `NaN≠NaN`; cannot be special-cased without diverging from\n  golden.\n- **NaN (case 13 f32 [nan,nan])**: `erf(NaN)=NaN`, `0.5*NaN*(1+NaN)=NaN`. IEEE\n  propagation through `asc2.erf`/mul ⇒ matches golden. Same residual NaN-comparison\n  caveat as above.\n- **Zero (case 14 [0,0] tanh)**: `erf/tanh(0)=0`, `y=0`. Exact.\n- **Precision**: f16 thresh `2^-10≈9.7e-4`, bf16 `2^-7≈7.8e-3`, f32 `2^-13≈1.2e-4`.\n  All f16/bf16 cases compute in f32 then cast back ⇒ strictly more accurate than the\n  golden's f16/bf16 path; f32 cases use the cancellation-free erf/tanh forms with no\n  `exp(+arg)` (no overflow) and no `log(1+tiny)` (no flush). `erf`/`tanh` are bounded,\n  so no guard-band logic is needed.\n\n## 7. Anti-cheat constraints\n\n- ALL math (`erf`, `tanh`, `*`, `+`, casts) lives inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on\n  the NPU. Host does only: `ensure_npu_platform()`, `.contiguous()`, `torch.empty_like`,\n  `.numel()`, `.dtype`, string dispatch, launch, return.\n- No torch compute/math ops anywhere (`torch.mul`, `F.gelu`, `a+b`, `.to(dtype)` on\n  device data, `torch.cat/clone/sum`, `x.sigmoid()`…). No `data_ptr` caching.\n- `approximate` string is consumed on the host only (never passed into a kernel — str\n  is not a supported param type anyway).\n- Output is a fresh contiguous NPU tensor (`torch.empty_like(x)`) with golden's exact\n  shape/dtype; no views of the input.\n- Constants precomputed module-level; no `import`/`math.*` inside jit.\n\n## 8. Local validation ladder\n\nNo NPU and no pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu installed locally (per task.md). Ladder:\n\n1. **Syntax only** — `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (allowed; checks AST, no\n   imports execute). Run after writing candidate.\n2. **Worker static contract check** — requires the CANNBench worker runtime; not\n   runnable here ⇒ treated as `suspected`, deferred to remote.\n3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** (skill `references/local-validation.md`) — requires\n   the pinned `pyasc-v2-source`; not installed here ⇒ `suspected`, deferred. UB\n   overflow (§5) is a runtime launch failure that this gate would NOT catch anyway;\n   the conservative tiles in §4 are chosen to avoid it a priori.\n4. **camodel numerical compare vs golden.py** — no local camodel ⇒ `suspected`.\n5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — the only acceptance/performance oracle; remote, invoked\n   by the official harness.\n\nEvidence label for the design phase: `suspected` (no local compile/numerical evidence\npossible). Promotion to `verified-local-compile` / `verified-camodel` requires steps\n2–4, which are unavailable in this environment.\n\n## 9. Open implementation notes (for candidate.py, next phase)\n\n- Two kernels: `_gelu_erf_kernel` and `_gelu_tanh_kernel`, identical signature\n  `(x: asc.GlobalAddress, out: asc.GlobalAddress, size: int, num_tiles: int,\n   tile: asc.ConstExpr[int])`.\n- Host `gelu(x, approximate=\"none\")`: `ensure_npu_platform()`; `if not x.is_contiguous():\n  x = x.contiguous()`; `out = torch.empty_like(x)`; `size = x.numel()`; empty→return;\n  branch on `approximate` (`\"none\"`→erf, `\"tanh\"`→tanh; any other value ⇒ assert, since\n  spec allows only these two); pick tile per §4; `ceildiv` via `asc.ceildiv`;\n  `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`; launch; return `out`.\n- `x.is_contiguous()` / `.contiguous()` / `.numel()` / `.dtype` are metadata/views —\n  allowed by the anti-cheat whitelist.\n\nDESIGN_DONE","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":183,"totalLines":183,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/design.md","time":{"start":1788349345675,"end":1788349345680}},"id":"prt_061ed6d3d001kyT6l75aj0FYbR","sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","messageID":"msg_061ed62c2001nXJqo8f5ijtwTT"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788349346464,"sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_0685329b2774425aa967b687","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n2: \n3: Kernel design (grid-stride variant):\n4:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n5:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n6:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n7:     spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n8:     store.\n9:   - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n10:     param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n11:       * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n12:             y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n13:       * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n14:             y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n15:   - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n16:     on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n17:   - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n18:     1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n19:   - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n20:     values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n21:     identical-form evaluation.\n22: \"\"\"\n23: \n24: import math\n25: \n26: import torch\n27: \n28: import asc\n29: import asc2\n30: \n31: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n32: \n33: _C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n34: _C0_TANH = math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n35: _K_TANH = 0.044715\n36: \n37: _ERF_TILE = 2048\n38: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n39: _TANH_TILE = 1024\n40: _MAX_CORES = 72\n41: _ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n42: \n43: \n44: @asc2.jit\n45: def _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n46:                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n47:                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n48:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n49:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n50:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n51:                         unroll_factor=2):\n52:         off = t * tile_size\n53:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n54:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n55:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n56:         s = xf * _C1_ERF\n57:         e = asc2.erf(s)\n58:         one = e + 1.0\n59:         hx = xf * 0.5\n60:         yf = hx * one\n61:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n62: \n63: \n64: @asc2.jit\n65: def _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n66:                       size: int, num_tiles: int,\n67:                       tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n68:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n69:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n70:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n71:                         unroll_factor=2):\n72:         off = t * tile_size\n73:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n74:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n75:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n76:         x2 = xf * xf\n77:         x3 = x2 * xf\n78:         a = x3 * _K_TANH\n79:         b = xf + a\n80:         c = b * _C0_TANH\n81:         th = asc2.tanh(c)\n82:         one = th + 1.0\n83:         hx = xf * 0.5\n84:         yf = hx * one\n85:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n86: \n87: \n88: def gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n89:     \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n90:     ensure_npu_platform()\n91:     assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n92:         f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n93:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n94:         x = x.contiguous()\n95:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n96:     size = x.numel()\n97:     if size == 0:\n98:         return out\n99:     if approximate == \"none\":\n100:         if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n101:             tile = _ERF_TILE\n102:         else:\n103:             tile = _NARROW_TILE\n104:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n105:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n106:         _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n107:     else:\n108:         tile = _TANH_TILE\n109:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n110:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n111:         _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n112:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 112 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n    identical-form evaluation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n_C0_TANH = math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n_K_TANH = 0.044715\n\n_ERF_TILE = 2048\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_TANH_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n_ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                     tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        s = xf * _C1_ERF\n        e = asc2.erf(s)\n        one = e + 1.0\n        hx = xf * 0.5\n        yf = hx * one\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        x2 = xf * xf\n        x3 = x2 * xf\n        a = x3 * _K_TANH\n        b = xf + a\n        c = b * _C0_TANH\n        th = asc2.tanh(c)\n        one = th + 1.0\n        hx = xf * 0.5\n        yf = hx * one\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n        f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if approximate == \"none\":\n        if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n            tile = _ERF_TILE\n        else:\n            tile = _NARROW_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    else:\n        tile = _TANH_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":112,"totalLines":112,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/gelu-generate/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788349346457,"end":1788349346463}},"id":"prt_061ed710c0011QIHCsdeKTWYxF","sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","messageID":"msg_061ed62c2001nXJqo8f5ijtwTT"}}
