Static review: anti-cheat compliance","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Fix candidate.py if needed","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run python3 -m py_compile candidate.py","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"3 todos","time":{"start":1788349608933,"end":1788349608935}},"id":"prt_061f164b0001wKNQSHCry6Zk78","sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","messageID":"msg_061f0592b001Rx3LefI3c2dPBu"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788349608952,"sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","part":{"id":"prt_061f1538a0012hpwJrumSYG1Eu","messageID":"msg_061f0592b001Rx3LefI3c2dPBu","sessionID":"ses_f9e12b54bffe5CzyalueGVMpfG","type":"text","text":"**Numerical stability — PASS**\n\n- **erf mode**: Direct hardware `asc2.erf` for `y = 0.5*x*(erf(x/√2)+1)`. No explicit `exp(+arg)` overflow risk. Saturation gives correct limits. ✓\n- **tanh mode**: `tanh(C0*(x+K*x³))` — x³ max at f32 cases (|x|≤100, 100³=1e6 within f32). For large |x|, tanh saturates → y→x or y→0, cancellation is benign (golden computes same formula). ✓\n- **Inf (case 12, bf16)**: IEEE propagation: +inf→+inf, -inf→NaN (matches golden). ✓\n- **NaN (case 13, f32)**: erf(NaN)*0.5*NaN → NaN, IEEE propagation. ✓\n- **Zero (case 14)**: Exact in both modes. ✓\n- **Precision**: All f16/bf16 compute in f32 then cast back (strictly more accurate than golden's in-dtype path). f32 threshold 1.2e-4 is generous for identical-formula computation. ✓\n\n","time":{"start":1788349600650,"end":1788349608949}}}
